# Banner

Every file opens with exactly four comment lines. C uses `//`. Scripts and text use `#`. A `.py` shebang may occupy line 1; the banner then starts on line 2. `CMakePresets.json` and `LICENSE` have no banner.

    // re_arena.h - bump allocator giving one malloc and one free per command.
    // Module: util (C11).
    // Owns: bump-pointer blocks, chunk list, reset and free.
    // Depends: none. No I/O, no globals, thread-unsafe by design.

Slots, in order:

1. Basename, then one-line purpose. The gate requires the filename on this line.
2. `Module: <name> (<language>).` including the period.
3. `Owns: ...`
4. `Depends: ...` and the architectural constraint on the same line.

Keep each banner line under 100 columns. clang-format wraps a long line 3 or 4 onto line 5, and rule 2 then fails.

`#pragma once` follows the banner in every header, exactly once.
